---
title: Icon and logo
navTitle: Icon and logo
order: 3
description: The SVG icon sprite and the flower mark.
---
{% from "docs.njk" import example, usage %}
{% from "components/icon/icon.njk" import icon %}
{% from "components/logo/logo.njk" import logo, flowerMark %}
<header class="docs-header">
  <p class="docs-eyebrow">Component · Partial</p>
  <h1>Icon and logo</h1>
  <p class="docs-lede">Line icons drawn on a 24px grid with a 1.5 stroke, all in one inline SVG sprite that the base layout includes once. They take on the colour of the text around them.</p>
</header>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="use">
  <h2 id="use">Use it</h2>
  {% set code %}{% raw %}{% from "components/icon/icon.njk" import icon %}
{{ icon("bag") }}                          {# decorative: hidden from screen readers #}
{{ icon("bag", { label: "Basket" }) }}     {# meaningful on its own #}
{{ icon("close", { size: "md" }) }}

{% from "components/logo/logo.njk" import logo %}
{{ logo({ href: "/" }) }}{% endraw %}{% endset %}
  {{ usage(code) }}
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="icons">
  <h2 id="icons">Icons</h2>
  {% set names = ["bag", "close", "plus", "minus", "menu", "check", "alert", "arrow-right", "arrow-left", "zoom", "chevron-down", "instagram", "mail"] %}
  {% set ex %}{% for n in names %}<span class="docs-swatch">{{ icon(n, { size: "md" }) }}<code>{{ n }}</code></span>{% endfor %}{% endset %}
  {{ example("All icons, md size", ex, { noCode: true }) }}
  {% set ex %}{{ icon("bag") }} {{ icon("bag", { size: "md" }) }}{% endset %}
  {{ example("Sizes: sm (default) and md", ex) }}
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="logo">
  <h2 id="logo">Logo</h2>
  <p>The flower mark, redrawn as SVG from <code>flower-mark.png</code> so it stays sharp at every size. The stem uses <code>--ds-color-brand-mark</code> and the centre uses <code>--ds-color-brand-mark-centre</code>. <strong>To check:</strong> PIP, please compare it with the original artwork. If there's a source vector, it should replace this trace.</p>
  {% set ex %}{{ logo({ href: "/" }) }}{% endset %}
  {{ example("Logo", ex) }}
  {% set ex %}<span style="display:flex;gap:var(--ds-space-inline-md);align-items:end"><img src="/assets/images/flower-mark.png" alt="Original PNG" width="44" height="80"> {{ flowerMark() | replace('class="ds-logo__mark"', 'class="ds-logo__mark" style="block-size: 80px"') | safe }}</span>{% endset %}
  {{ example("Original PNG next to the SVG trace", ex, { noCode: true }) }}
  {% set ex %}{{ logo({ href: "/" }) }}{% endset %}
  {{ example("On the pink band", ex, { band: true }) }}
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="a11y">
  <h2 id="a11y">Accessibility</h2>
  <ul class="docs-list">
    <li>Icons are <code>aria-hidden</code> by default. If an icon is the only content of a button or link, give that button or link an <code>aria-label</code>, or pass <code>label</code> to the icon.</li>
    <li>The logo's accessible name is “Calico Melton”, from its visible text.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
